A REAL BUG in my refactor, caught by the regression test:

Actual skip list: `'quantum/q-1 (unknown adapter dialect: quantum-chat) quantum/q-1 (unknown provider: quantum)'`

BOTH reasons are reported! The helper reports the dialect skip AND the caller still falls to the generic `(unknown provider: ...)` skip.

Why? Look at the flow: helper returns null for the unknown-dialect case → caller's `viaRegistry == null` → falls through to `if (spec == null)` → spec is still null (catalog missed, registry leg null) → reports `(unknown provider: ...)`. The original inline code RETURNED null immediately from _buildEntry on the dialect path; my helper only signals "no answer" and the caller can't distinguish "registry silent" from "dialect skip already reported".

The helper needs a tri-state or the caller must skip the generic report when the registry leg already answered. Options:

A. Return a sentinel record: helper returns `(ModelRef, ProviderSpec)?` for success, and for the two null paths... need distinction. Use an enum-ish result or a bool out-param — clunky.

B. Restructure: helper RETURNS the spec-or-null decision differently — e.g. helper takes over the whole skip handling: pass `skipped` and have it return `(ModelRef, ProviderSpec)?` where null ALWAYS means "already reported; return null from _buildEntry" — i.e., move the generic unknown-provider skip INTO the helper too! Then _buildEntry:

```dart
var spec = resolveCliProviderSpec(ref.provider, honorBuildFilter: true);
if (spec == null) {
  final viaRegistry = _registryLeg(ref, skipped, onUnknownProvider: onUnknownProvider);
  if (viaRegistry != null) {
    (ref, spec) = viaRegistry;
  } else {
    return null;  // skip already reported by the leg
  }
```

And _registryLeg reports the generic `(unknown provider: ...)` reason when no entry matches, the dialect reason when the entry's apiType is unknown, and returns the pair on success. All skip+degrade logic lives in ONE place; _buildEntry's CC drops further (the generic-skip if disappears from it): _buildEntry decisions in region: spec==null + viaRegistry!=null → and the later generic if is REMOVED (−1 more decision → CC 10). The gh-760 comment moves to the helper.

